  "hypothesis": "H88-MVRD: Concealed and unmapped Quaternary geothermal faults in Nevada produce (1) asymmetric 1 m LiDAR / 10 m 3DEP monoclinal bajada flexures (downface_max - upface_max and steep_frac * aspect_coherence) without stream-wall symmetric dipoles, (2) 60-degree hanging-wall magnetic analytic-signal & magnetite-destruction troughs (mag_anom, TMI, TMI_up150) paired with hydrothermal U/Th & U/K redox-clay cross-gradients, and (3) collinear 1.5-3.0 km strand continuity along physical tectonic strike. Replacing uniform prior mixing with a spatially adaptive completeness deficit gate w_blind(d_vis) (zero within 350 m of mapped traces, rising smoothly in blind basins > 1-2.5 km) plus Bayes-exact dual-expectation calibration and 2.05 px knight's-move Dinkelbach CELF allocation recovers unmapped basin/piedmont fault strands while eliminating visible-fault flank bleed.",
  "mechanism": "85-feature completeness-gated ensemble combining (1) 44-ch dip-back-projected competition + DOE GDR #1391 2 m thermal advection + paleoshoreline-decontaminated physics, (2) 18 new MVRD physical channels (magnetic analytic signal, volcanic remanence discrepancy, 60-deg dip-projected analytic signal, 1 m LiDAR monoclinal polarity & cross-scarp jump, 10 m 3DEP bajada scarp index & steep-slope concentration, 300 m piedmont-propagated tectonic knickzone power & chi divide jump, and GeoDAWN U/Th & U/K hydrothermal redox-clay cross-gradients), and (3) 23 strictly fold-visible relay/step-over features, fused via spatial completeness gating w_blind(d_vis), sharpened along physical spin-2 strike tensor, and allocated via unmodified gems57.emit.dinkelbach_allocate (min_spacing_px=2.05).",
